0,Ormuri - WikipediaORMURI Phoneme Inventory — IPA LookupThe Sound of Indo-European Music (Compilation) - YouTubeIndo-European Music - playlist by kinoid | SpotifyOLAC Record: Indo-Iranian Frontier Languages; Vol. I; Parachi ...Indo-European Music (UPDATED) - YouTubeOLAC resources in and about the Ormuri language,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ormuri,"Although not trained in the classical European linguistic tradition, he is regarded as one of the most important indigenous contributors to modern Ormuri documentation. ORMURI (Indo-European) has 31 phonemes. Browse its full IPA sound inventory and compare it to other languages. Sep 8, 2019 · In this video, I compiled music from all the major Indo-European languages. I hope you enjoy these great songs! Indo-European Music · Playlist · 485 songs · 19 likes The Rosetta Project: A Long Now Foundation Library of Human Language. Collection of Indo-European Music! Ormuri Interlinear Texts: texts 1-51 from Logar, Afghanistan, recorded by V.A. Efimov. Hawbaker, Jeremy (editor); Baart, Joan L. G. (editor); Efimov, Valentin Aleksandrovič (transcriber). 2011.",Ormuri,Indo-European
1,"Ormuri - Simple English Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia",https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ormuri,"June 11, 2022 - Ormuri (Persian: ارموری · ) is an East Iranian language spoken in the city of Kaniguram in Pakistan. It may also be spoken by a few people in Logar, Afghanistan. It is notable for its unusual sound inventory. This includes a voiceless alveolar trill and voiced and unvoiced alveolo-palatal ...",Ormuri,Indo-European
